  <p class="lead-text">
    If a judge, the Mississippi Department of Public Safety, or a reinstatement letter told you that you need an "SR-22," you're probably wondering what that is and how fast you can get one. Here's a plain-English explanation.
  </p>

  <h2>1. What Is an SR-22?</h2>
  <p>
    Despite the name, an SR-22 <strong>isn't a type of insurance</strong>. It's a certificate of financial responsibility that your insurance company files with the state to prove you carry at least Mississippi's minimum required liability coverage.
  </p>
  <p>
    You buy an auto insurance policy as usual, and your insurer attaches the SR-22 filing to it and submits it to the Mississippi Department of Public Safety on your behalf.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Who Needs an SR-22 in Mississippi?</h2>
  <p>
    The state typically requires an SR-22 after certain serious violations or license actions, such as:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>A DUI or DWI conviction</li>
    <li>Being caught driving without insurance, or causing an accident while uninsured</li>
    <li>Driving with a suspended or revoked license</li>
    <li>Certain serious moving violations or repeated offenses</li>
    <li>Reinstating a license after a suspension or revocation</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Your court paperwork or reinstatement notice will tell you whether an SR-22 is required.
  </p>

  <h2>3. How Long Do You Need It?</h2>
  <p>
    In Mississippi, an SR-22 is commonly required for <strong>three years</strong>, but the exact period depends on your specific violation and order. Always confirm your required filing period with the Mississippi Department of Public Safety or your reinstatement paperwork.
  </p>
  <div class="callout-box">
    <h3>⚠️ Don't Let Your Policy Lapse</h3>
    <p>If your policy cancels or lapses while an SR-22 is required, your insurer is required to notify the state, and your license can be suspended again. That can restart the clock. Setting up automatic payments is one of the simplest ways to protect yourself.</p>
  </div>

  <h2>4. How Much Does an SR-22 Cost?</h2>
  <p>
    The filing itself usually carries a small one-time fee from the insurance company. The bigger cost is the <strong>insurance premium</strong>, because the violation that triggered the SR-22 typically raises your rates.
  </p>
  <p>
    That's exactly why shopping matters. Carriers price high-risk drivers very differently, and not every company files SR-22s at all. As an independent agency, we can compare several carriers at once instead of you calling around.
  </p>

  <h2>5. No Car? You May Need a Non-Owner SR-22</h2>
  <p>
    If you don't own a vehicle but need your license reinstated, a <strong>non-owner policy with an SR-22</strong> can satisfy the requirement. It provides liability coverage when you drive a car you don't own and is often less expensive than a standard policy.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Moving Out of Mississippi?</h2>
  <p>
    If you move to another state while your Mississippi SR-22 requirement is active, you generally still need to maintain it for the full period. Talk to us before you move so your coverage and filing stay in place.
  </p>

  <h2>7. How to Get Your SR-22 Filed</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Call us at (662) 638-3777 or request a quote online.</li>
    <li>We'll compare carriers that file SR-22s in Mississippi.</li>
    <li>Once you choose a policy and make your first payment, the carrier files the SR-22 with the state.</li>
    <li>Keep your policy active for the entire required period.</li>
  </ol>

  <div class="tip-box">
    <h3>✅ Rebuild Your Rates Over Time</h3>
